{"pages":[{"w":612.0,"h":792.0,"s":[[13.889,2.206,18.17,3.8,3.431,"EQUINOX"],[13.889,5.306,14.953,1.205,1.078,"Q U A N T I T A T I V E"],[69.444,2.807,16.401,1.643,1.471,"Commodities Research"],[69.444,4.27,11.266,1.46,1.307,"12 November 2026"],[13.889,10.995,7.45,3.651,3.268,"Gold"],[13.889,14.731,41.745,2.373,2.124,"A quarter off the record; the Fed is still hiking"],[13.889,20.845,52.931,1.809,1.634,"Gold settled at $4,000 on 11 November, 25% below its 29 January record close"],[13.889,22.289,52.931,1.809,1.634,"of $5,318. The Federal Reserve raised rates in September, for the first time since"],[13.889,23.733,52.964,1.809,1.634,"2023, to 3.75-4.00%, two members voted for more in October, and October CPI"],[13.889,25.177,52.951,1.809,1.634,"rose 0.4%. The 10-year real yield is 2.78%, 89bp above its level at the record,"],[13.889,26.621,52.964,1.809,1.634,"and the dollar index is up 7%. Our model, fitted to weekly changes over 2006-"],[13.889,28.065,52.931,1.809,1.634,"23, takes 3.8% off gold for each 100bp on real yields and 1.0% for each 1% on"],[13.889,29.509,40.114,1.809,1.634,"the dollar. Together they explain 9 points of the 25-point fall."],[13.889,31.995,52.936,1.809,1.634,"The rest is a premium deflating. From end-2023 to the record gold rose 157%;"],[13.889,33.439,52.931,1.809,1.634,"rates, the dollar and gold’s 8% a year drift account for 24%. A third of the"],[13.889,34.883,52.931,1.809,1.634,"excess has gone, yet gold still trades 62% above the model path of $2,470 and"],[13.889,36.328,52.966,1.809,1.634,"9% above the 1980 peak in today’s dollars. Holders are paying for the official"],[13.889,37.772,52.931,1.809,1.634,"bid: central banks bought 675t in nine months, 6% more than a year earlier. Two"],[13.889,39.216,52.934,1.809,1.634,"cautions. Only 120t of the third quarter’s 321t was reported, and the first quarter"],[13.889,40.684,52.966,1.809,1.634,"was revised from 244t to 57t. And price-sensitive buyers have stepped back:"],[13.889,42.128,37.541,1.809,1.634,"jewellery fell 17% and bars and coins 19% in the quarter."],[13.889,44.59,52.931,1.809,1.634,"We rate gold Neutral with a Dec-27 target of $4,400, 10% above the price"],[13.889,46.034,52.931,1.809,1.634,"(ladder: −5% to +15%), the weighted value of three cases. Base (50%): the Fed"],[13.889,47.502,52.966,1.809,1.634,"raises twice more, real yields ease to 2.4% and the premium holds, $4,530. Bull"],[13.889,48.946,52.951,1.809,1.634,"(25%): the Fed reverses, real yields return to 1.9% and the premium rebuilds,"],[13.889,50.39,52.951,1.809,1.634,"$5,310. Bear (25%): real yields reach 3.25% and half the premium goes, $3,260."],[13.889,51.834,52.936,1.809,1.634,"Light futures positioning is no reason to buy: the nine times since 2009 it"],[13.889,53.278,52.936,1.809,1.634,"reached the bottom fifth of its three-year range, gold returned 4% over the next"],[13.889,54.722,52.934,1.809,1.634,"year against 11% for all weeks. In rupees the fall is 21%, cushioned by May’s"],[13.889,56.167,34.783,1.809,1.634,"duty rise to 15%; reversing it would cost holders 8%."],[13.889,58.654,13.042,1.643,1.471,"Price Performance"],[14.451,68.023,2.306,1.022,0.915,"3,500"],[14.451,66.721,2.306,1.022,0.915,"4,000"],[14.451,65.409,2.306,1.022,0.915,"4,500"],[14.451,64.109,2.306,1.022,0.915,"5,000"],[14.451,62.807,2.306,1.022,0.915,"5,500"],[14.451,61.495,2.306,1.022,0.915,"6,000"],[14.451,60.195,2.306,1.022,0.915,"6,500"],[18.321,68.717,2.796,1.022,0.915,"Jan 26"],[23.029,68.717,2.796,1.022,0.915,"Apr 26"],[27.898,68.717,2.47,1.022,0.915,"Jul 26"],[32.506,68.717,2.96,1.022,0.915,"Oct 26"],[17.504,69.888,4.439,1.275,1.111,"Gold ($/oz)"],[24.724,69.888,9.893,1.275,1.111,"Gold in rupees (rebased)"],[20.2,71.048,1.972,1.387,1.209,"YTD"],[25.376,71.048,1.433,1.387,1.209,"1m"],[30.0,71.048,1.433,1.387,1.209,"3m"],[34.446,71.048,1.984,1.387,1.209,"12m"],[14.91,72.114,2.063,1.387,1.209,"USD"],[19.495,72.114,2.597,1.387,1.209,"-7.8%"],[24.12,72.114,2.597,1.387,1.209,"-5.1%"],[28.744,72.114,